  urldate       = {2026-10-24},
  note          = {The quaternion exponential, Exp(phi u) = [cos(phi/2); u sin(phi/2)] (its Eq. 101, Section 2.4.3), and its zeroth-order integration with the rate at the end of the step held over it, q_{n+1} = q_n (x) q{omega_{n+1} dt} (Eq. 216, Section 4.6.1), written there for a rate in the body frame; a world-frame rate's kinematics, qdot = omega_G (x) q / 2, and the frames' relation, omega_G = R omega_L (Eqs. 201 and 204, Section 4.5). rigid_inertial's q' = exp(dt omega') q, with omega' the world-frame rate after the step, is that step written with the world-frame rate: q (x) Exp(R^T omega' dt) = Exp(omega' dt) (x) q. Hamilton's convention, (w, x, y, z), body to world, as MIME's (Section 3).},
}
